      "writtenOn": "2022-07-26T14:44:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "[matrix OP scalar] is component-wise for most ops but is not component-wise for multiplication... it does a standard matrix multiply.\n\nOur no-op-elimination code only runs for square matrices (see `^` mark elsewhere) because yeah, it\u0027s not necessarily a no-op for a non-square matrix. I haven\u0027t thought it through 100% but I think it could be boiled down to a matrix-resize ctor. However I don\u0027t think it\u0027s going to be common to see matrix-resizes expressed as multiplications against non-square identity matrices! \n\nThis test code is only focused on the square matrix case because that\u0027s all we actually optimize. Non-square mats should pass through unaffected.\n\nAll that being said I\u0027m happy to rephrase this comment--what do you want it to say?",
